specifies a bidirectional mapping between an external IP netblock
and  an internal IP netblock.  A rule specifies that IP addresses
are to be changed as the packet traverses  the  given  interface.
This technique allows one or more IP addresses on the translating
host to support network traffic for a larger range of machines on
